<title>SPAIN: Spain details 1997 March budget deficit.</title>
<headline>Spain details 1997 March budget deficit.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economy Ministry gave the following detailed figures of Spain's state deficit on cash basis</p>
<p> BUDGET OPERATIONS	   MAR 97	FEB 97	   MAR 96</p>
<p> Revenues			668.6	 2,062.2	    646.1</p>
<p> Expenditure		 1,329.5	 1,886.0	  1,338.3</p>
<p> Deficit/surplus	    -660.9	  +176.2	   -692.2</p>
<p> Deficit to date	    -861.2	  -200.3	   -6.28.1</p>
<p>GBR yr to date</p>
<p>or deficit on national</p>
<p> account basis		-836.0	  -286.5	   na</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures relate to central government finances only. GBR = government borrowing requirement.</p>
<p>Spain gave also the following table to explain the differences between the deficit on cash basis and the deficit on National account basis (in the first quarter):</p>
<p>   1. Deficit on cash basis			     -861.2</p>
<p>   2.  Adjustments					    25.2</p>
<p>	 - variation in accrued revenues</p>
<p>    and expenditures					 462.4</p>
<p>	 - Adj for state debt interest payments	 20.9</p>
<p>	 - Privatisations				   -375.0</p>
<p>	 - Others						-83.1</p>
<p>    PSBR (1 + 2)					    -836.0</p>
<p>    GDP extimation for 1997			   78,860.0</p>
<p>    As a percentage of GDP				   1.1%</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
